<h1>camera_get_view_border_y</h1>
<p>This function can be used to retrieve the y (vertical) border value set for the given camera, which can be set in the room properties (see <a href="../../../../The_Asset_Editors/Room_Properties/Room_Properties.htm#h">Cameras And Viewports</a>) or via the function <span class="inline3_func"><a href="camera_set_view_border.htm">camera_set_view_border</a></span>). The return value will be in pixels.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">camera_get_view_border_y(camera_id)</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>camera_id</td>
<td><span data-keyref="Type_ID_Camera"><a target="_blank" href="camera_create.htm">Camera ID</a></span></td>
<td>The unique camera ID value returned when you created the camera</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">var xb = camera_get_view_border_x(view_camera[0]);<br/>
var yb = camera_get_view_border_y(view_camera[0]);<br/>
if xb != 200 || yb != 200<br/>
{<br/>
    camera_set_view_border(view_camera[0], 200, 200);<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above code retrieves the xborder and yborder values of the camera assigned to view port[0] and then checks this to see if it matches the given value. If it does not then the view camera is set to the given value.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
